      "message": "Super nit-picky, but something about this phrasing feels slightly off to me. The call `myBlender.eval(s, d)` blends s with d, but it doesn\u0027t blend _into_ anything. Same with `SkShaders::Blend`. These just evaluate the blend between s and d. There\u0027s no \"blending into\" anything unless it\u0027s the blend-step of a paint (or the primitive-color blend, a wacky special case).\n\nI think the only issue here is the comment; there\u0027s nothing wrong with the code itself. I\u0027m also wondering if `kChildOutput` just means \"no destination\" or if there\u0027s something else to it?\n\nAt any rate this nit-pick is just about comment phrasing... the code itself seems fine.",
